{"kind":"request","text":"State and ratify a scoped inbound charter for the GitHub connector, because the current one authorizes nothing in particular and the connector now refuses it.\n\nThe ratified inbound charter f696c18a has a null body. It names no connector, no repository owner or name, and no workroom actor. Until now that did not matter, because the connector checked only that the named statement was present, ratified and live — which meant it would have run against any repository at all while pointing at that ratification as its doorstep.\n\nThe connector now requires the charter body to name four things and refuses to run unless each matches what its process was told to do: `connector` (github), `owner`, `repo`, and `actor` (the connector's workroom actor). An empty body is refused rather than read generously, on the grounds that a charter which does not say what it charters cannot bound anything. So this is a live blockage, not a theoretical one: the connector cannot run until a scoped charter exists.\n\nThis needs an operator's signature and a ratification, so it is not mine to do. Stating the charter is the act that fixes, once, who may state an admission clause at all; the clauses themselves then take force on statement without further ratification, which is the arrangement Hugh described.\n\nWorth deciding while stating it: whether one charter covers one repository or a set. One repository per charter keeps the blast radius of a retirement small and makes the four-field check exact, at the cost of a charter per repository. That is the shape the connector currently assumes.","body":{"conditions":"A charter for the GitHub connector's inbound half is stated by an operator and ratified, with a body naming connector=github, the repository owner and name, and the connector's workroom actor; the connector run with --charter pointing at it, and with matching --owner, --repo-name and --as, passes its doorstep check rather than being refused; the superseded charter f696c18a is retired, so no ratified statement remains that would look like a doorstep while bounding nothing; whether a charter covers one repository or several is decided and the reason recorded, since the connector's current check assumes one.","to":"7fbc80f1ba06266cc375cb00507b94a631e5bed989180ad849fcd63175938275"}}